Rejig: remember the gaps Rejig placed, per iPhone, and send them back with every write.
Applies to ios_homescreen/state.py, snapshots.py, api.py, workflow.py, model.py, report.py,
ui/app.py, ui/session.py and the editor's static files from
https://github.com/YakupEmreYerli/ios-homescreen at commit
97649547dbc44295e451c6bf130a87404481e10c, after Rejig's other patches. A read never shows
gaps, so Rejig keeps the pins of each verified write in DATA_DIR/pins.json, bound to each
page as the verifying read showed it. A later read gets them back only on pages that still
read the same, and a write's backup and rollback carry them, so Restore puts gaps back.
In the editor, dropping an app on an empty cell (or "Place in a spot...") pins it, and
dragging it into the flow (or "Move back in line") unpins it. Pin changes count as changes,
with their own wording. Apply writes only the plan that was reviewed. A damaged or
unsaved pins.json, or a write the phone was not read back after, stops writes, so stale
gaps are never sent. No code is adapted from
homescreen-mcp here; pinned-gaps.patch credits the method. ios-homescreen is MIT-licensed,
Copyright (c) 2026 Yakup Emre Yerli (full notice in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). This patch is
MIT.

